{"global_index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1306", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To bypass US Munitions Export Laws, the creator of the PGP published all the source code in book form. \n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A} \n\nThe creator of PGP (Pretty Good Privacy), Phil Zimmermann, did indeed publish the source code in book form to legally distribute it and bypass U.S. export restrictions on encryption software. This act highlighted the complexities of export laws concerning cryptographic tools. As a result, the publication in book form was both a strategic legal maneuver and a way to share the software freely.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 179}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "\\boxed{A} \n\nThe creator of PGP (Pretty Good Privacy), Phil Zimmermann, did indeed publish the source code in book form to legally distribute it and bypass U.S. export restrictions on encryption software. This act highlighted the complexities of export laws concerning cryptographic tools. As a result, the publication in book form was both a strategic legal maneuver and a way to share the software freely.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.33e-05}}
