{"global_index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_1015", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the name given to layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (ISO) model?\n\nOptions: \nA. Transport\nB. Data link\nC. Session\nD. Network\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model is known as the Transport layer, which is responsible for end-to-end communication and data flow control between hosts. The other options refer to different layers: Data Link is layer 2, Session is layer 5, and Network is layer 3.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 102, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 174}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Layer 4 of the Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model is known as the Transport layer, which is responsible for end-to-end communication and data flow control between hosts. The other options refer to different layers: Data Link is layer 2, Session is layer 5, and Network is layer 3.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.85e-05}}
{"global_index": "OpenTDB_Science: Computers_3613", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All program codes have to be compiled into an executable file in order to be run. This file can then be executed on any machine.\n\nOptions: \nA. True\nB. False\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nNot all programs need to be compiled into an executable file; interpreted languages run directly through an interpreter without the need for compilation. Additionally, compiled programs may not be portable across different systems due to dependencies on specific architectures or operating systems. Therefore, the statement is false.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 100, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 158}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nNot all programs need to be compiled into an executable file; interpreted languages run directly through an interpreter without the need for compilation. Additionally, compiled programs may not be portable across different systems due to dependencies on specific architectures or operating systems. Therefore, the statement is false.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.98e-05}}
{"global_index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_2943", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you could fold a piece of paper in half 50 times, its' thickness will be 3/4th the distance from the Earth to the Sun.\n\nOptions: \nA. False\nB. True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. When you fold a piece of paper in half repeatedly, the thickness doubles with each fold, leading to an exponential increase in thickness. After 50 folds, the thickness would indeed exceed the distance from the Earth to the Sun, making the statement true.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 106, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 165}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. When you fold a piece of paper in half repeatedly, the thickness doubles with each fold, leading to an exponential increase in thickness. After 50 folds, the thickness would indeed exceed the distance from the Earth to the Sun, making the statement true.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.13e-05}}
{"global_index": "OpenTDB_Science: Mathematics_1530", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many zeptometres are inside one femtometre?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1,000,000,000\nB. 1,000,000\nC. 1000\nD. 10\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "One femtometre (fm) is equal to \\(10^{-15}\\) metres, and one zeptometre (zm) is equal to \\(10^{-21}\\) metres. To convert femtometres to zeptometres, you can divide the exponent: \\(10^{-15} / 10^{-21} = 10^{6}\\). Therefore, there are \\(1,000,000\\) zeptometres in one femtometre. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 110, "output_tokens": 110, "total_tokens": 220}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "One femtometre (fm) is equal to \\(10^{-15}\\) metres, and one zeptometre (zm) is equal to \\(10^{-21}\\) metres. To convert femtometres to zeptometres, you can divide the exponent: \\(10^{-15} / 10^{-21} = 10^{6}\\). Therefore, there are \\(1,000,000\\) zeptometres in one femtometre. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.25e-05}}
