{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_67", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The MSS is typically set by first determining the length of the largest link-layer frame that can be sent by the local sending host (the so-called( )), and then will fit into a single link-layer frame. \n\nOptions: \nA. Maximum segment size (MSS)\nB. MTU\nC. Sequence number\nD. Check sum\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). The Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) refers to the size of the largest packet that can be sent over a network link, which influences the determination of the Maximum Segment Size (MSS) for protocols like TCP. The MSS is derived from the MTU by accounting for the header sizes, ensuring that data fits within a single link-layer frame.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 133, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 213}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). The Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) refers to the size of the largest packet that can be sent over a network link, which influences the determination of the Maximum Segment Size (MSS) for protocols like TCP. The MSS is derived from the MTU by accounting for the header sizes, ensuring that data fits within a single link-layer frame.", "ground_truth": "B", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.795e-05}}
{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_540", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The U.S.CAN-SPAM Act: ( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. makes spamming illegal.\nB. requires commercial email senders to identify themselves.\nC. has dramatically cut down spamming.\nD. does not override state anti-spamming laws.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The CAN-SPAM Act requires commercial email senders to identify themselves and includes other regulations related to email marketing. While it aims to reduce spam, it has not completely eliminated it and does not override state laws that can be more stringent.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 114, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 170}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The CAN-SPAM Act requires commercial email senders to identify themselves and includes other regulations related to email marketing. While it aims to reduce spam, it has not completely eliminated it and does not override state laws that can be more stringent.", "ground_truth": "B", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.07e-05}}
