{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_523", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the ( ) model of informed consent, personal information cannot be collected until the consumer specifically agrees that his or her data can be collected. \n\nOptions: \nA. opt-in\nB. opt-out\nC. P3P\nD. PGP\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. In the opt-in model of informed consent, consumers must explicitly agree to the collection of their personal information before it can be gathered. This contrasts with the opt-out model, where information may be collected unless the consumer chooses to decline consent.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 171}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. In the opt-in model of informed consent, consumers must explicitly agree to the collection of their personal information before it can be gathered. This contrasts with the opt-out model, where information may be collected unless the consumer chooses to decline consent.", "ground_truth": "A", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.0849999999999996e-05}}
