{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_72", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Because TCP only acknowledges bytes up to the first missing byte in the stream, TCP is said to provide ( ) acknowledgements. \n\nOptions: \nA. Cumulative\nB. Selective\nC. Single\nD. Negative\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. TCP provides cumulative acknowledgements, which means that it acknowledges all bytes received successfully up to the first byte that is missing. This approach allows TCP to efficiently manage flow control and retransmissions.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 109, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 155}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. TCP provides cumulative acknowledgements, which means that it acknowledges all bytes received successfully up to the first byte that is missing. This approach allows TCP to efficiently manage flow control and retransmissions.", "ground_truth": "A", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.395e-05}}
