{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_600", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following level of managers develop short and medium-range plans, schedules and budgets and specify the policies, procedures and business objectives for their subunits of the company? ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. Strategic\nB. Tactical\nC. Operational\nD. Front Line\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Tactical managers are responsible for developing short and medium-range plans and specifying policies, procedures, and business objectives for their specific subunits. This level of management acts as a bridge between strategic goals set by top management and the operational activities of front-line managers.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 118, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 177}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Tactical managers are responsible for developing short and medium-range plans and specifying policies, procedures, and business objectives for their specific subunits. This level of management acts as a bridge between strategic goals set by top management and the operational activities of front-line managers.", "ground_truth": "B", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.31e-05}}
{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_603", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In which of the following types of analysis, the value of only one variable is changed repeatedly, and the resulting changes on other variables are observed. ( )\n\nOptions: \nA. What-if analysis\nB. Sensitivity analysis\nC. Goal seeking analysis\nD. None of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Sensitivity analysis. This type of analysis focuses on determining how different values of an independent variable will impact a particular dependent variable under a given set of assumptions. It helps in understanding the variability and robustness of a model. \n\nThus, the answer is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 181}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is B. Sensitivity analysis. This type of analysis focuses on determining how different values of an independent variable will impact a particular dependent variable under a given set of assumptions. It helps in understanding the variability and robustness of a model. \n\nThus, the answer is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "B", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.415e-05}}
{"global_index": "ArcMMLU_609", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The set of processes developed in an organization to create, gather, store, transfer, and apply knowledge, best describes:( ).\n\nOptions: \nA. organizational learnings\nB. knowledge management\nC. organizational memory\nD. knowledge assets\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Knowledge management refers to the systematic processes that an organization uses to create, gather, store, transfer, and apply knowledge. This encompasses all activities that help in the effective use of knowledge to improve efficiency and innovation within the organization.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 165}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Knowledge management refers to the systematic processes that an organization uses to create, gather, store, transfer, and apply knowledge. This encompasses all activities that help in the effective use of knowledge to improve efficiency and innovation within the organization.", "ground_truth": "B", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.904999999999999e-05}}
