{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9141", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A session symmetric key between two parties is used\n\nOptions: \nA. Twice\nB. Until one of the parties terminates the session\nC. For a predetermined length of time\nD. Until a new key is generated\nE. Only when both parties agree\nF. Conditions dependant\nG. For a specific number of transactions\nH. Multiple times\nI. Until the key is compromised\nJ. Only once\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. A session symmetric key is typically used for the duration of a session between two parties, and it is terminated when one of the parties decides to end the session. This allows for secure communication within that specific interaction.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 149, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 202}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. A session symmetric key is typically used for the duration of a session between two parties, and it is terminated when one of the parties decides to end the session. This allows for secure communication within that specific interaction.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.415e-05}}
