{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9171", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An integer overflow occurs when\n\nOptions: \nA. an integer expression's result \"wraps around\"; instead of creating a very large number, a very small (or negative) number ends up getting created\nB. an integer is used as if it was a pointer\nC. an integer is used to access a buffer outside of the buffer's bounds\nD. there is no more space to hold integers in the program\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. An integer overflow occurs when a calculation produces a result that exceeds the maximum value that can be stored in an integer variable, causing it to \"wrap around\" to a smaller negative number or zero. This is a fundamental issue in programming related to how integers are represented in memory.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 212}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. An integer overflow occurs when a calculation produces a result that exceeds the maximum value that can be stored in an integer variable, causing it to \"wrap around\" to a smaller negative number or zero. This is a fundamental issue in programming related to how integers are represented in memory.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.0599999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9172", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A packet filter firewall filters at the\n\nOptions: \nA. Network or transport layer\nB. Application layer only\nC. Physical Layer\nD. Data link layer\nE. Application or transport\nF. Session layer\nG. Transport layer only\nH. Network interface layer\nI. All layers of the OSI model\nJ. Presentation layer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. A packet filter firewall typically operates at the network layer (Layer 3) and the transport layer (Layer 4) of the OSI model, filtering packets based on IP addresses, protocols, and port numbers. It does not function at the application layer or below.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 198}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. A packet filter firewall typically operates at the network layer (Layer 3) and the transport layer (Layer 4) of the OSI model, filtering packets based on IP addresses, protocols, and port numbers. It does not function at the application layer or below.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.805e-05}}
