{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9269", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Another term for out-of-distribution detection is?\n\nOptions: \nA. precision-recall detection\nB. underfitting detection\nC. bias-variance tradeoff detection\nD. regularization detection\nE. one-class detection\nF. overfitting detection\nG. cross-validation detection\nH. background detection\nI. train-test mismatch robustness\nJ. anomaly detection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Out-of-distribution detection refers to the method of identifying data points that differ significantly from the training dataset, which is commonly associated with anomaly detection. This process is important in ensuring models can robustly handle unexpected or novel data inputs.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 197}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Out-of-distribution detection refers to the method of identifying data points that differ significantly from the training dataset, which is commonly associated with anomaly detection. This process is important in ensuring models can robustly handle unexpected or novel data inputs.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.52e-05}}
