{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9389", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Define the term \"debugging.\"\n\nOptions: \nA. Debugging is the process of creating bugs.\nB. Debugging refers to the enhancement of a program's performance without the need to fix faults.\nC. Debugging means deploying a program.\nD. Debugging is the compilation of source code into executable programs.\nE. Debugging is the process of testing a program.\nF. Debugging involves the systematic elimination of a computer virus from a program.\nG. Debugging is the initial design and development phase of a program.\nH. Debugging is the process of optimizing the user interface of a program.\nI. Debugging a program means the modification of programs, throughout its lifetime, in order to fix the faults that produce unacceptable or unexpected results.\nJ. Debugging is the routine updating of software to add new features.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Debugging specifically refers to the process of identifying and fixing faults in a program that lead to unexpected behavior or errors. This definition captures the essence of debugging, which is vital for software development and maintenance.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 278}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Debugging specifically refers to the process of identifying and fixing faults in a program that lead to unexpected behavior or errors. This definition captures the essence of debugging, which is vital for software development and maintenance.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.375e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9398", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 3-way, set-associative cache is\n\nOptions: \nA. only effective when more than 3 processes are running alternately on the processor\nB. possible only with write-through\nC. one in which each main memory word can be stored at any of 4 cache locations\nD. possible only with write-back\nE. effective only if 3 or fewer processes are running alternately on the processor\nF. one in which each cache can store 3 main memory words\nG. one in which each main memory word can be stored at any of 3 cache locations\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. A 3-way set-associative cache means that each block of main memory can be mapped to any one of 3 different cache lines (or locations) within a specific set. This allows for greater flexibility than direct-mapped caches but is not limited to any specific number of processes running concurrently.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 184, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 253}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. A 3-way set-associative cache means that each block of main memory can be mapped to any one of 3 different cache lines (or locations) within a specific set. This allows for greater flexibility than direct-mapped caches but is not limited to any specific number of processes running concurrently.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.9e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9403", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Buffer-overflow may remain as a bug in apps if __________ are not done fully.\n\nOptions: \nA. boundary hacks\nB. system updates\nC. firewall settings\nD. server resets\nE. software installations\nF. buffer checks\nG. boundary checks\nH. virus scans\nI. memory checks\nJ. data backups\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Buffer-overflow vulnerabilities can persist in applications if proper boundary checks are not implemented, as these checks help ensure that data written to buffers does not exceed allocated limits. Without sufficient boundary checks, malicious actors can exploit these oversights, leading to potential breaches or crashes.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 193}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Buffer-overflow vulnerabilities can persist in applications if proper boundary checks are not implemented, as these checks help ensure that data written to buffers does not exceed allocated limits. Without sufficient boundary checks, malicious actors can exploit these oversights, leading to potential breaches or crashes.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.6399999999999995e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9412", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Write a skeletal format of C programs.\n\nOptions: \nA. [data types] [macros] main ( ) {{ [execution flow] }} [helper functions]\nB. [function prototypes] [globals] main ( ) {{ [control structures] }} [subroutines]\nC. [constant declarations] [internals] main ( ) {{ [program statements] }} [additional methods]\nD. [constant declarations] [externals] main ( ) {{ [program statements] }} [additional functions]\nE. [variables] [functions] main ( ) {{ [program logic] }} [additional classes]\nF. [module imports] [class definitions] main ( ) {{ [data processing] }} [external functions]\nG. [preprocessor directives] main ( ) {{ [program code] }} [libraries]\nH. [variable declarations] [externals] main ( ) {{ [program conditions] }} [additional functions]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. \n\nA skeletal format of C programs typically includes preprocessor directives, the main function, and the necessary libraries for the program to function. The format in option G encapsulates the essential components of standard C programming.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 251, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 302}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. \n\nA skeletal format of C programs typically includes preprocessor directives, the main function, and the necessary libraries for the program to function. The format in option G encapsulates the essential components of standard C programming.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.824999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9420", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A user enters a Web address in a browser, and a request for a file is sent to a Web server. Which of the following best describes how the file is sent to the user?\n\nOptions: \nA. The server attempts to connect directly to the user's computer. If the connection is successful, the entire file is sent. If the connection is unsuccessful, an error message is sent to the user.\nB. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The user's browser must request each packet randomly until all packets are received.\nC. The server compresses the file into a single packet for transmission. The user's browser decompresses the packet upon receipt.\nD. The server repeatedly attempts to connect directly to the user's computer until a connection is made. Once the connection is made, the entire file is sent.\nE. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The packets must be reassembled upon receipt.\nF. The file is broken into packets for transmission. The user's browser must request each packet in order until all packets are received.\nG. The server sends each packet to the user's computer, which must confirm receipt of each packet before the next one is sent.\nH. The file is sent in separate sections, which are downloaded sequentially by the user's browser.\nI. The server sends the file in a continuous stream to the user's browser, which buffers the stream for viewing.\nJ. The server sends the entire file in one large transmission to the user's browser.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct choice is \\boxed{E}. Files are typically broken into smaller packets for transmission over the internet, and the receiving system (the user's browser) needs to reassemble these packets to reconstruct the original file. This process ensures effective and reliable transmission across potentially unstable networks.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 356, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 411}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct choice is \\boxed{E}. Files are typically broken into smaller packets for transmission over the internet, and the receiving system (the user's browser) needs to reassemble these packets to reconstruct the original file. This process ensures effective and reliable transmission across potentially unstable networks.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.64e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9431", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: TCP protocol is responsible (among other things) for\n\nOptions: \nA. Ensuring secure and encrypted communication between machines\nB. Enabling communication between different network protocols\nC. Routing packets through the network\nD. Managing the energy consumption of network devices\nE. Dealing with differences among operating system architectures\nF. Reliable delivery of large (multi-packet) messages between machines that are not necessarily directly connected\nG. Managing the physical layer of network communication\nH. Providing a user interface for network communication\nI. Reliable delivery of packets between directly connected machines\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. The TCP protocol is designed to provide reliable delivery of large messages over a network, ensuring that data sent between machines can be reassembled correctly even if it is split into multiple packets. It does not inherently handle encryption, routing, or energy management, nor does it concern itself directly with the physical layer or user interfaces.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 178, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 250}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. The TCP protocol is designed to provide reliable delivery of large messages over a network, ensuring that data sent between machines can be reassembled correctly even if it is split into multiple packets. It does not inherently handle encryption, routing, or energy management, nor does it concern itself directly with the physical layer or user interfaces.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.989999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9434", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let A be a finite set with m elements, and let B be a finite set with n elements. The number of distinct functions mapping A into B is\n\nOptions: \nA. m^n\nB. n!/m!\nC. (n + m)!\nD. m!/(m - n)!\nE. n!/(n - m)!\nF. m!/(n!(m - n)!)\nG. n!\nH. m!/n!\nI. n^m\nJ. n!/(m!(n - m)!)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The number of distinct functions mapping a finite set \\( A \\) with \\( m \\) elements to a finite set \\( B \\) with \\( n \\) elements is given by \\( n^m \\). This is because each element in \\( A \\) can be mapped to any of the \\( n \\) elements in \\( B \\), and there are \\( m \\) such choices. Therefore, the correct answer is \\( \\boxed{I} \\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 174, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 267}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The number of distinct functions mapping a finite set \\( A \\) with \\( m \\) elements to a finite set \\( B \\) with \\( n \\) elements is given by \\( n^m \\). This is because each element in \\( A \\) can be mapped to any of the \\( n \\) elements in \\( B \\), and there are \\( m \\) such choices. Therefore, the correct answer is \\( \\boxed{I} \\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.19e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9435", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: _ refers to a model that can neither model the training data nor generalize to new data.\n\nOptions: \nA. overfitting\nB. data fitting\nC. all of the above\nD. perfect fitting\nE. precise fitting\nF. underfitting\nG. ideal fitting\nH. good fitting\nI. misfitting\nJ. best-fitting\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Underfitting refers to a model that is too simplistic to capture the underlying structure of the training data, resulting in poor performance both on the training set and in generalization to new data. This means that the model cannot accurately model either the training or the new data.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 202}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Underfitting refers to a model that is too simplistic to capture the underlying structure of the training data, resulting in poor performance both on the training set and in generalization to new data. This means that the model cannot accurately model either the training or the new data.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8649999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9436", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| VGGNets have convolutional kernels of smaller width and height than AlexNet's first-layer kernels. Statement 2| Data-dependent weight initialization procedures were introduced before Batch Normalization.\n\nOptions: \nA. Both Statement 1 and Statement 2 are Not Given\nB. Statement 1 is Not Given and Statement 2 is True\nC. True, True\nD. Statement 1 is False and Statement 2 is Not Given\nE. True, False\nF. False, False\nG. Statement 1 is True and Statement 2 is Not Given\nH. False, True\nI. Statement 1 is Not Given and Statement 2 is False\nJ. Statement 1 is Not Given and Statement 2 is Not Given\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. VGGNets use smaller convolutional kernels (3x3) compared to AlexNet's first-layer kernels (11x11), making Statement 1 true. Additionally, data-dependent weight initialization procedures were introduced before the advent of Batch Normalization, making Statement 2 also true.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 286}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. VGGNets use smaller convolutional kernels (3x3) compared to AlexNet's first-layer kernels (11x11), making Statement 1 true. Additionally, data-dependent weight initialization procedures were introduced before the advent of Batch Normalization, making Statement 2 also true.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.26e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9445", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which Nmap scan is does not completely open a TCP connection?\n\nOptions: \nA. TCP connect\nB. SCTP INIT scan\nC. SYN stealth scan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. A SYN stealth scan, also known as a half-open scan, doesn't complete the TCP handshake and thus does not fully open a TCP connection. In contrast, both TCP connect (A) and SCTP INIT scan (B) establish full connections.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 96, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 154}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. A SYN stealth scan, also known as a half-open scan, doesn't complete the TCP handshake and thus does not fully open a TCP connection. In contrast, both TCP connect (A) and SCTP INIT scan (B) establish full connections.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.9199999999999997e-05}}
