{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9118", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain the 'END OF FILE Condition' method of ending a Explain the 'END OF FILE Condition' method of ending a programin PL/I.\n\nOptions: \nA. The end-file condition occurs when a special end-of-file character is encountered within the file's data.\nB. The end-file condition occurs when the file is not found\nC. The end-file condition occurs when the operating system signals the end of a file due to a timeout.\nD. The end-file condition occurs when the file is manually closed by the user during the execution of the program.\nE. The end-file condition occurs when an attempt is made to acquire data from the input file after the last data from the file has already been read.\nF. The end-file condition occurs when the file reaches a certain size limit during data writing.\nG. The end-file condition occurs when the file is corrupted\nH. The end-file condition occurs when the file's read permission is revoked while the program is running.\nI. The end-file condition is triggered by a specific keyword written into the file.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. The 'END OF FILE Condition' in PL/I indicates that there are no more data records to be read from the input file, which occurs when an attempt is made to read beyond the last piece of data. This condition is important for controlling the flow of a program that processes file input.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 276, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 343}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. The 'END OF FILE Condition' in PL/I indicates that there are no more data records to be read from the input file, which occurs when an attempt is made to read beyond the last piece of data. This condition is important for controlling the flow of a program that processes file input.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.16e-05}}
