{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9180", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain and discuss why the branch and link register (BALR) instruction is usually one of the most important instruc-tions of the IBM/360-370 computers?\n\nOptions: \nA. BALR instruction is important because it is used for data encryption and security purposes.\nB. BALR instruction is important because it increases the graphical processing capabilities of the computer.\nC. BALR instruction is important because it directly manipulates arithmetic operations.\nD. BALR instruction is important because it simplifies the programming process.\nE. BALR instruction is important because it serves as a primary instruction for input/output operations.\nF. BALR instruction is important because it speeds up the program.\nG. BALR instruction is important because it allows for base address loading into the base register of the program, which is crucial for the program's execution.\nH. BALR instruction is important because it enables the computer to perform multitasking more efficiently.\nI. BALR instruction is important because it allows for immediate value assignment to multiple registers.\nJ. BALR instruction is important because it reduces memory usage.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The BALR (Branch and Link Register) instruction is essential in IBM/360-370 computers as it enables the setting of the program's base register, facilitating proper address calculations for program execution. This capability is crucial for managing program control flow and handling subroutine calls effectively.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 278, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 342}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The BALR (Branch and Link Register) instruction is essential in IBM/360-370 computers as it enables the setting of the program's base register, facilitating proper address calculations for program execution. This capability is crucial for managing program control flow and handling subroutine calls effectively.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.01e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9181", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A sign of a good computer programmer is the ability to write a program which minimizes storage usage. The IBM 360/370 computers provide us with the DSECT and CSECT statements . How do they enable us to becomebetter programmers ?\n\nOptions: \nA. They optimize the program by automatically correcting coding errors.\nB. They allow for faster execution of programs.\nC. The statements create a cloud-based backup of the program for additional storage.\nD. The DSECT and CSECT statements allow for the definition and use of many variables without allocating storage space for them all at once, minimizing storage usage.\nE. The statements divide the program into smaller, independent sections that can be loaded as needed.\nF. They enable multithreading capabilities.\nG. DSECT and CSECT statements provide a framework for artificial intelligence integration.\nH. They increase the program’s compatibility with various operating systems.\nI. They streamline the user input process to reduce the amount of code required.\nJ. They enhance the graphic interface of the program.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The DSECT and CSECT statements allow programmers to define data structures and code sections without allocating all necessary storage upfront, which effectively minimizes storage usage. This capability enhances memory efficiency by loading only the needed parts of the program into storage at any given time.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 274, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 335}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The DSECT and CSECT statements allow programmers to define data structures and code sections without allocating all necessary storage upfront, which effectively minimizes storage usage. This capability enhances memory efficiency by loading only the needed parts of the program into storage at any given time.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.769999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9182", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain briefly the background and applications of BASIC computer language.\n\nOptions: \nA. BASIC was developed by Microsoft to enhance the Windows operating system.\nB. BASIC was created by IBM as a language to program mainframe computers and has limited use today due to its complexity.\nC. BASIC stands for \"Business Acquisition and System Integration Code\" and is used mainly in the corporate finance sector.\nD. BASIC is an advanced programming language used mainly for developing complex scientific simulations and models.\nE. BASIC is an acronym for \"Binary Algorithmic Scientific Instruction Code\" and is used primarily in data analysis.\nF. BASIC was developed in the 1950s as a language for artificial intelligence research.\nG. BASIC is a language developed at Dartmouth College in the 1960s to make the computer more accessible and easy to use. It is widely used in science, business, and engineering due to its simplicity and similarity to English and algebra.\nH. BASIC was developed in the 1980s to simplify computer programming.\nI. BASIC is a language developed in the late 1970s for the exclusive use in graphical user interface design.\nJ. BASIC is a language primarily used in the field of arts and literature.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. BASIC was developed at Dartmouth College in the 1960s with the intention of making computing more accessible to students and non-technical users. Its simplicity and resemblance to English and algebra contributed to its widespread use in various fields, including science, business, and engineering.", "token_usage":