{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9217", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Explain the TRAILER CARD method of stopping a computer job, i.e., a program.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Trailer Card method uses a serial number on the first card to stop a program.\nB. The Trailer Card method uses a specific phrase typed into the console to signal the end of a job.\nC. The Trailer Card method requires a specific card to be inserted physically into the computer.\nD. The Trailer Card method involves sending an electronic signal through a network to stop the program.\nE. The Trailer Card method employs a magnetic tape marker to indicate the end of a program.\nF. The Trailer Card method uses a unique number on the last card in the data section of a program card deck to signal the end of a job.\nG. The Trailer Card method utilizes a timer that automatically stops the program after a set duration.\nH. The Trailer Card method involves pressing a designated key on the computer's keyboard to terminate the job.\nI. The Trailer Card method requires the operator to manually switch off the computer to end the job.\nJ. The Trailer Card method uses a special code to pause a program.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. The Trailer Card method uses a unique number on the last card in the data section of a program card deck to signal the end of a job, making it distinct and ensuring that the program understands when to terminate. This was a common practice in early computing using punched cards.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 286, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 349}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. The Trailer Card method uses a unique number on the last card in the data section of a program card deck to signal the end of a job, making it distinct and ensuring that the program understands when to terminate. This was a common practice in early computing using punched cards.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.07e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9238", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1| The softmax function is commonly used in mutliclass logistic regression. Statement 2| The temperature of a nonuniform softmax distribution affects its entropy.\n\nOptions: \nA. False, False\nB. True, Statement 2 is not related to Statement 1\nC. False, Both statements are related to each other\nD. Statement 2 is true, but Statement 1 is irrelevant\nE. Statement 1 is true, but Statement 2 is irrelevant\nF. False, True\nG. True, False\nH. True, Both statements are unrelated to each other\nI. False, Statement 1 is not related to Statement 2\nJ. True, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). Both statements are true: the softmax function is indeed used in multiclass logistic regression, and the temperature of a nonuniform softmax distribution does influence its entropy. Since both statements are correct and relevant, option J is the best choice.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 267}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). Both statements are true: the softmax function is indeed used in multiclass logistic regression, and the temperature of a nonuniform softmax distribution does influence its entropy. Since both statements are correct and relevant, option J is the best choice.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.659999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9254", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How are tracers useful as a debugging aid?\n\nOptions: \nA. Tracers automatically correct errors in the source code\nB. Tracers help to encrypt the program\nC. Tracers compile the program into machine language\nD. Tracers help to optimize the code\nE. Tracers help to reduce the execution time of a program\nF. Tracers predict future bugs in the program based on past trends\nG. Tracers obfuscate the code to protect it from reverse engineering\nH. Tracers increase the processing speed of the program\nI. Tracers help locate bugs by analyzing and executing real machine instructions one at a time, allowing complete internal program inspection.\nJ. Tracers enhance the graphical user interface of the program\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Tracers are debugging tools that allow developers to analyze program execution by monitoring the execution of instructions, which helps in locating bugs and understanding the program's behavior more effectively. This real-time inspection is crucial for diagnosing issues during program development.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 279}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Tracers are debugging tools that allow developers to analyze program execution by monitoring the execution of instructions, which helps in locating bugs and understanding the program's behavior more effectively. This real-time inspection is crucial for diagnosing issues during program development.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.705e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9255", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Illustrate transfer of control in a PL/I program, usingGOTO statements.\n\nOptions: \nA. The GOTO statement in PL/I program doesn't alter the processing sequence.\nB. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program resumes processing at the next function or procedure.\nC. The GOTO statement in PL/I program alters the processing sequence, discontinues the normal sequential execution and processing resumes at a point that is indicated by a label.\nD. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program creates a subroutine call to a labeled section of the code.\nE. The GOTO statement continues the sequential execution.\nF. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program is used to repeat the execution of a loop from the beginning.\nG. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program is a conditional statement that only executes if a specified condition is true.\nH. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program causes the program to terminate immediately.\nI. The GOTO statement in PL/I program processing resumes at a point without a label.\nJ. The GOTO statement in a PL/I program pauses execution and waits for user input before continuing.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The GOTO statement in PL/I alters the normal sequential execution of a program, allowing control to jump to a specified label, thus changing the flow of execution. This mechanism can be used for various programming constructs but can also make code harder to follow if overused.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 294, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 356}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The GOTO statement in PL/I alters the normal sequential execution of a program, allowing control to jump to a specified label, thus changing the flow of execution. This mechanism can be used for various programming constructs but can also make code harder to follow if overused.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.13e-05}}
