{"global_index": "MMLUPro_philosophy_9756", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which early battle led to the conversion of Mecca?\n\nOptions: \nA. The Battle of Badr\nB. The Battle of Yamama\nC. The Battle of Hunayn\nD. The Battle of Mut'ah\nE. The Battle of Tabuk\nF. The Battle of Khaybar\nG. The Battle of Camel\nH. The Battle of the Trench\nI. The Battle of Ta'if\nJ. The Battle of Uhud\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The Battle of Hunayn was significant in the early Islamic expansion and contributed to the eventual conversion of Mecca, as it occurred shortly after the Muslims took control of the city and led to further consolidation of Islamic influence in the region. The battle helped to solidify Muhammad's position and enabled the spread of Islam among various tribes.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 160, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 234}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The Battle of Hunayn was significant in the early Islamic expansion and contributed to the eventual conversion of Mecca, as it occurred shortly after the Muslims took control of the city and led to further consolidation of Islamic influence in the region. The battle helped to solidify Muhammad's position and enabled the spread of Islam among various tribes.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.84e-05}}
