h means the argument is invalid.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\), as it presents a counterexample when \\( G \\) is true and \\( H \\) is false, showing the argument is invalid.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010725}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_51", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following propositions is an immediate (one-step) consequence in PL of the given premises?\n(N ⊃ ~O) ⊃ (O ∨ Q)\nP ⊃ (N ⊃ ~O)\nN ⊃ P\n\nOptions: \nA. P\nB. N ⊃ ~O\nC. O ∨ Q\nD. ~P\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine an immediate consequence of the premises, we can analyze the implications. The second premise, \\(P \\supset (N \\supset \\neg O)\\), suggests that if \\(P\\) is true, then \\(N \\supset \\neg O\\) must also be true. The correct answer is \\(B. N \\supset \\neg O\\) because it is directly obtained from premise 2 when \\(P\\) is assumed true.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 250}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine an immediate consequence of the premises, we can analyze the implications. The second premise, \\(P \\supset (N \\supset \\neg O)\\), suggests that if \\(P\\) is true, then \\(N \\supset \\neg O\\) must also be true. The correct answer is \\(B. N \\supset \\neg O\\) because it is directly obtained from premise 2 when \\(P\\) is assumed true.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.475e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_57", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use indirect truth tables to determine whether each set of propositions is consistent. If the set is consistent, choose an option with a consistent valuation. (There may be other consistent valuations.)\n(T ⊃ U) ⊃ (W ⊃ U)\nT ⊃ ~(U ⊃ X)\n(T ⊃ ~X) ⊃ W\n\nOptions: \nA. Inconsistent\nB. Consistent. Consistent valuation when U, W, and X are true and T is false\nC. Consistent. Consistent valuation when W and X are true and T and U are false\nD. Consistent. Consistent valuation when T and U are true and W and X are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the consistency of the given set of propositions, we look for a valuation that satisfies all propositions simultaneously. Evaluating the valuations provided in the options, option B satisfies the conditions of the propositions while maintaining logical truth across each statement. Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 270}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the consistency of the given set of propositions, we look for a valuation that satisfies all propositions simultaneously. Evaluating the valuations provided in the options, option B satisfies the conditions of the propositions while maintaining logical truth across each statement. Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.75e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_8", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the following propositions is an immediate (one-step) consequence in PL of the given premises?\n~E ⊃ ~F\nG ⊃ F\nH ∨ ~E\nH ⊃ I\n~I\n\nOptions: \nA. E ⊃ F\nB. F ⊃ G\nC. H ⊃ ~E\nD. ~H\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine which proposition is an immediate consequence of the premises, we can analyze the implications logically. Given the premises, we have \"H ⊃ I\" and \"~I,\" which leads to the conclusion that \"H\" must be false (i.e., ~H) because if H were true, I would also be true, contradicting the premise. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 145, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 230}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine which proposition is an immediate consequence of the premises, we can analyze the implications logically. Given the premises, we have \"H ⊃ I\" and \"~I,\" which leads to the conclusion that \"H\" must be false (i.e., ~H) because if H were true, I would also be true, contradicting the premise. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.275e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_87", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Construct a complete truth table for the following argument. Then, using the truth table, determine whether the argument is valid or invalid. If the argument is invalid, choose an option which presents a counterexample. (There may be other counterexamples as well.)\n~X ⊃ Y\nY ⊃ Z\n~Z / ~X\n\nOptions: \nA. Valid\nB. Invalid. Counterexample when X, Y, and Z are true\nC. Invalid. Counterexample when Y and Z are true and Z is false\nD. Invalid. Counterexample when X is true and Y and Z are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To construct the truth table, we evaluate the premises and conclusion. The argument is invalid if there is a situation where the premises are true and the conclusion is false. In this case, when \\( X \\) is true, \\( Y \\) is false, and \\( Z \\) is false, both premises are true but the conclusion \\( \\sim X \\) is false, making option D a valid counterexample.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 98, "total_tokens": 288}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To construct the truth table, we evaluate the premises and conclusion. The argument is invalid if there is a situation where the premises are true and the conclusion is false. In this case, when \\( X \\) is true, \\( Y \\) is false, and \\( Z \\) is false, both premises are true but the conclusion \\( \\sim X \\) is false, making option D a valid counterexample.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.73e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_97", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use indirect truth tables to determine whether the following argument is valid. If the argument is invalid, choose an option which presents a counterexample. (There may be other counterexamples as well.)\nL ⊃ [(M ∨ ~N) ⊃ O]\n(N ⊃ O) ⊃ (~P ⊃ Q)\nR ⊃ ~Q / L ⊃ (R ⊃ P)\n\nOptions: \nA. Valid\nB. Invalid. Counterexample when L, M, O, Q, and R are true and N and P are false\nC. Invalid. Counterexample when L, N, O, Q, and R are true and M and P are false\nD. Invalid. Counterexample when L, N, and R are true and M, O, P, and Q are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the validity of the argument using indirect truth tables, we evaluate the premises and the conclusion. An invalid argument will have all premises true while the conclusion is false. Upon testing the given counterexamples, option B demonstrates an invalid scenario where the conclusion does not follow from the true premises.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 237, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 306}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the validity of the argument using indirect truth tables, we evaluate the premises and the conclusion. An invalid argument will have all premises true while the conclusion is false. Upon testing the given counterexamples, option B demonstrates an invalid scenario where the conclusion does not follow from the true premises.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.695e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_30", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use indirect truth tables to determine whether each set of propositions is consistent. If the set is consistent, choose an option with a consistent valuation. (There may be other consistent valuations.)\nA ⊃ (~B ∨ C)\nC ⊃ D\nA ∨ (B · ~D)\nA ≡ (B ⊃ D)\n\nOptions: \nA. Inconsistent\nB. Consistent. Consistent valuation when A and D are true and B and C are false\nC. Consistent. Consistent valuation when A, B, and D are true and C is false\nD. Consistent. Consistent valuation when C and D are true and A and B are false\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the consistency of the set of propositions, we can analyze the statements. By testing the proposed valuations, option B (A is true, D is true, B is false, C is false) maintains the truth of all propositions: A ⊃ (~B ∨ C) is true, C ⊃ D is true, A ∨ (B · ~D) is true, and A ≡ (B ⊃ D) holds true, confirming consistency. Other options do not fulfill all required conditions simultaneously. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 122, "total_tokens": 328}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the consistency of the set of propositions, we can analyze the statements. By testing the proposed valuations, option B (A is true, D is true, B is false, C is false) maintains the truth of all propositions: A ⊃ (~B ∨ C) is true, C ⊃ D is true, A ∨ (B · ~D) is true, and A ≡ (B ⊃ D) holds true, confirming consistency. Other options do not fulfill all required conditions simultaneously. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\box