{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_88", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  S Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some kind people help some endangered species. (Ex: x is endangered; Kx: x is kind; Px: x is a person; Sx: x is a species; Hxy: x helps y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (∃x){{(Kx • Px) • (∃y)[(Ey • Sy) • Hxy]}}\nB. (∃x)(∃y){{[(Kx • Sx) • (Ey • Py)] • Hxy}}\nC. (∃x)(∃y){{[(Kx • Sx) • (Ey • Py)] • Hyx}}\nD. (∃x)(∃y){{[(Kx • Px) • (Ey • Sy)] ⊃ Hxy}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). This option correctly reflects that there exists some kind person (Kx) who helps (Hyx) some endangered species (Sy), while also adhering to the proper quantifiers and structure of the statement. The other options either misrepresent the relationships or fail to properly connect the relevant subjects and predicates.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 308}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). This option correctly reflects that there exists some kind person (Kx) who helps (Hyx) some endangered species (Sy), while also adhering to the proper quantifiers and structure of the statement. The other options either misrepresent the relationships or fail to properly connect the relevant subjects and predicates.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.769999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_124", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some CEO is wealthier than everyone. (Cx: x is a CEO; Px: x is a person; Wxy: x is wealthier than y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (∃x)[Cx • (∀y)(Py • Wxy)]\nB. (∃x)[Cx ⊃ (∀y)(Py ⊃ Wxy)]\nC. (∃x)[Cx • (∀y)(Py ⊃ Wxy)]\nD. (∀x)[Px ⊃ (∃y)(Cy ⊃ Wxy)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). This option states that there exists some CEO \\(x\\) such that for all persons \\(y\\), \\(x\\) is wealthier than \\(y\\), which accurately captures the meaning of \"some CEO is wealthier than everyone.\" The use of the conjunction \\(•\\) indicates that both conditions must hold, aligning well with the statement's implications.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 273}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). This option states that there exists some CEO \\(x\\) such that for all persons \\(y\\), \\(x\\) is wealthier than \\(y\\), which accurately captures the meaning of \"some CEO is wealthier than everyone.\" The use of the conjunction \\(•\\) indicates that both conditions must hold, aligning well with the statement's implications.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.83e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_39", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. All jellybeans are sweeter than all fruit. (Fx: x is a fruit; Jx: x is a jellybean; Sxy: x is sweeter than y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (∀x)[Fx ⊃ (∀y)(Jy ⊃ Sxy)]\nB. (∀x)(∀y)[(Fx • Jy) • Sxy]\nC. (∀x)(∀y)[Sxy ⊃ (Fy • Jx)]\nD. (∀x)[Jx ⊃ (∀y)(Fy ⊃ Sxy)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). This option states that for all jellybeans \\(x\\), it holds that for all fruits \\(y\\), \\(x\\) is sweeter than \\(y\\), which captures the meaning of the statement \"All jellybeans are sweeter than all fruit\". The other options do not accurately reflect this relationship.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 191, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 262}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). This option states that for all jellybeans \\(x\\), it holds that for all fruits \\(y\\), \\(x\\) is sweeter than \\(y\\), which captures the meaning of the statement \"All jellybeans are sweeter than all fruit\". The other options do not accurately reflect this relationship.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.125e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_62", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use the following key to translate the given formula of PL to natural, English sentences.\nA: Marina reads a Percy Jackson book.\nB: Izzy plays Minecraft.\nC: Emily stops working.\nD: Russell makes dinner.\nE: Ashleigh stops by.\n~C ∨ D\n\nOptions: \nA. If Emily doesn't stop working then Russell makes dinner.\nB. Emily stops working unless Russell makes dinner.\nC. Emily stops working unless Russell doesn't make dinner.\nD. Emily doesn't stop working unless Russell makes dinner.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). The expression ~C ∨ D translates to \"either Emily does not stop working or Russell makes dinner,\" which aligns with the phrasing \"Emily stops working unless Russell makes dinner.\" Thus, option B accurately captures this logical relationship.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 168, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 225}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). The expression ~C ∨ D translates to \"either Emily does not stop working or Russell makes dinner,\" which aligns with the phrasing \"Emily stops working unless Russell makes dinner.\" Thus, option B accurately captures this logical relationship.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.9399999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_125", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. All children go to some school. (Cx: x is a child; Sx: x is a school; Gxy: x goes to y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (∀x)(∃y)[(Cx • Sy) • Gxy)\nB. (∀x)[Sx ⊃ (∃y)(Cy • Gxy)]\nC. (∀x)[Cx ⊃ (∃y)(Sy • Gxy)]\nD. (∀x)[Sx • (∃y)(Cy • Gxy)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option accurately reflects the statement \"All children go to some school\" by stating for every x (if x is a child), there exists some y such that y is a school and x goes to y. The structure captures the universal quantification of children and the existence of a school they attend.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 185, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 254}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option accurately reflects the statement \"All children go to some school\" by stating for every x (if x is a child), there exists some y such that y is a school and x goes to y. The structure captures the universal quantification of children and the existence of a school they attend.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.915e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_84", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Use the following key to translate the given formula of PL to natural, English sentences.\nA: Marina reads a Percy Jackson book.\nB: Izzy plays Minecraft.\nC: Emily stops working.\nD: Russell makes dinner.\nE: Ashleigh stops by.\n(A ∨ ~E) ≡ (D • ~B)\n\nOptions: \nA. Either Marina reading a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh not stopping by is a necessary condition for both Russell making dinner and Izzy not playing Minecraft.\nB. Either Marina reading a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh not stopping by is a necessary and sufficient condition for Russell making dinner and Izzy playing Minecraft.\nC. Marina reads a Percy Jackson book unless Ashleigh stops by if, and only if, both Russell makes dinner and Izzy doesn't play Minecraft.\nD. Either Marina reads a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh does not stop by just in case both Russell makes dinner and Izzy doesn't play Minecraft.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The expression (A ∨ ~E) ≡ (D • ~B) can be interpreted as stating that either Marina reads a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh does not stop by if and only if both conditions of Russell making dinner and Izzy not playing Minecraft hold true. This matches the structure of option D, making it the correct choice.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 254, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 335}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The expression (A ∨ ~E) ≡ (D • ~B) can be interpreted as stating that either Marina reads a Percy Jackson book or Ashleigh does not stop by if and only if both conditions of Russell making dinner and Izzy not playing Minecraft hold true. This matches the structure of option D, making it the correct choice.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.669999999999999e-05}}
