{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_17", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best translation into predicate logic. All planets are smaller than Jupiter. (j: Jupiter; Px: x is a planet; Sxy: x is smaller than y)\n\nOptions: \nA. (∃x)(Px • Sxj)\nB. (∀x)(Px • Sxj)\nC. (∀x)(Px ⊃ Sjx)\nD. (∀x)(Px ⊃ Sxj)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The statement \"All planets are smaller than Jupiter\" implies that for every object \\( x \\), if \\( x \\) is a planet, then \\( x \\) is smaller than Jupiter. This is accurately represented by the logical form \\( (∀x)(Px ⊃ Sxj) \\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 224}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The statement \"All planets are smaller than Jupiter\" implies that for every object \\( x \\), if \\( x \\) is a planet, then \\( x \\) is smaller than Jupiter. This is accurately represented by the logical form \\( (∀x)(Px ⊃ Sxj) \\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.51e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_1", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Select the best translation into predicate logic. David teaches Chris. (c: Chris; d: David; Txy: x teaches y)\n\nOptions: \nA. Tdc\nB. Tcd\nC. Tcc\nD. dTc\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct translation of \"David teaches Chris\" into predicate logic would be Tdc, where 'd' represents David and 'c' represents Chris. The first argument of the teaching predicate should denote the teacher, which is David in this case. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 173}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct translation of \"David teaches Chris\" into predicate logic would be Tdc, where 'd' represents David and 'c' represents Chris. The first argument of the teaching predicate should denote the teacher, which is David in this case. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.295e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_2", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Select the best English interpretation of the given proposition, using the following translation key: Ax: x is an apartment Hx: x is a house Lx: x is large Bxy: x is bigger than y (∃x)[(Ax • Lx) • (∃y)(Hy • Bxy)]\n\nOptions: \nA. Some large houses are bigger than some apartments.\nB. Some houses are bigger than all large apartments.\nC. Some large apartments are bigger than some houses.\nD. Some houses are bigger thatn some large apartments.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The proposition states that there exists an apartment \\(x\\) that is large (Lx) and there exists a house \\(y\\) such that the house \\(y\\) is bigger than that large apartment \\(x\\). Hence, it implies that some houses are bigger than some large apartments, which aligns with option D.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 176, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 253}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The proposition states that there exists an apartment \\(x\\) that is large (Lx) and there exists a house \\(y\\) such that the house \\(y\\) is bigger than that large apartment \\(x\\). Hence, it implies that some houses are bigger than some large apartments, which aligns with option D.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.26e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_83", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. Utilitarian theory is embarrassed by the possibility of utility monsters. A utility monster gets enormous gains in utility, greater than the utility lost by the sacrifices of others. The sacrifices of even large numbers of other people are outweighed by the gains of the utility monster. The theory seems to require that we all be sacrificed in the monste's maw in order to increase total utility. (Robert Nozick, Anarchy, State, and Utopia)\n\nOptions: \nA. Utilitarian theory is embarrassed by the possibility of utility monsters.\nB. A utility monster gets enormous gains in utility.\nC. A utility monster gets gains in utility greater than the utility lost by the sacrifices of others.\nD. The sacrifices of even large numbers of other people are outweighed by the gains of the utility monster.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The argument's main point is that utilitarian theory struggles with the implications of utility monsters, which is the overall conclusion regarding the theory's limitations. The other options present supporting statements but do not encapsulate the primary conclusion of the argument itself.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 287}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The argument's main point is that utilitarian theory struggles with the implications of utility monsters, which is the overall conclusion regarding the theory's limitations. The other options present supporting statements but do not encapsulate the primary conclusion of the argument itself.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.869999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_113", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. From a historical point of view, genetics is a young science. The principles that govern inheritance traits were described less than 150 years ago. Furthermore, around the turn of the twentieth century, the laws of inheritance were rediscovered. But even then, the importance of DNA was not really understood until the 1950s.\n\nOptions: \nA. But even then, the importance of DNA was not really understood until the 1950s.\nB. The importance of DNA was not really understood until the 1950s.\nC. From a historical point of view, genetics is a young science.\nD. The principles that govern inheritance traits were described less than 150 years ago.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option presents the main point of the argument by summarizing the historical context of genetics as a relatively new field. The other options provide supporting details rather than the central conclusion of the argument.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 255}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option presents the main point of the argument by summarizing the historical context of genetics as a relatively new field. The other options provide supporting details rather than the central conclusion of the argument.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.9399999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_26", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nThe restaurant serves pie or cheesecake or ice cream for dessert.\n\nOptions: \nA. P ∨ (C ∨ I)\nB. (P ∨ C) ∨ I\nC. P ∨ C ∨ I\nD. Options A and B\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The expression P ∨ C ∨ I accurately represents the idea that the restaurant serves any one of the desserts: pie (P), cheesecake (C), or ice cream (I) without any unnecessary grouping. Options A and B provide valid interpretations but are more complex than needed for the straightforward statement given.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 205}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The expression P ∨ C ∨ I accurately represents the idea that the restaurant serves any one of the desserts: pie (P), cheesecake (C), or ice cream (I) without any unnecessary grouping. Options A and B provide valid interpretations but are more complex than needed for the straightforward statement given.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.225e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_0", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. It is hard not to verify in our peers the same weakened intelligence due to emotions that we observe in our everyday patients. The arrogance of our consciousness, which in general, belongs to the strongest defense mechanisms, blocks the unconscious complexes. Because of this, it is difficult to convince people of the unconscious, and in turn to teach them what their conscious knowledge contradicts. (Sigmund Freud, The Origin and Development of Psychoanalysis)\n\nOptions: \nA. It is hard not to verify in our peers the same weakened intelligence due to emotions that we observe in our everyday patients.\nB. The arrogance of our consciousness, which in general, belongs to the strongest defense mechanisms, blocks the unconscious complexes.\nC. Because of this, it is difficult to convince people of the unconscious, and in turn to teach them what their conscious knowledge contradicts.\nD. It is difficult to convince people of the unconscious, and in turn to teach them what their conscious knowledge contradicts.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option encapsulates the main conclusion drawn from the argument regarding the challenges faced in convincing people about the unconscious and reconciling it with their conscious knowledge. The other options present premises or supporting statements rather than the conclusion of the argument.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 263, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 321}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option encapsulates the main conclusion drawn from the argument regarding the challenges faced in convincing people about the unconscious and reconciling it with their conscious knowledge. The other options present premises or supporting statements rather than the conclusion of the argument.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.424999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_119", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. We shouldn't abolish capital punishment. If we do, prisons will become more crowded. If prisons become more crowded, then we will have to build more prisons. And we don't want to build more prisons.\n\nOptions: \nA. We shouldn't abolish capital punishment.\nB. If we do, prisons will become more crowded.\nC. If prisons become more crowded, then we will have to build more prisons.\nD. We will have to build more prisons.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The conclusion of the argument is that \"We shouldn't abolish capital punishment.\" This statement directly expresses the main point the argument is trying to make, which is supported by the premises regarding the consequences of abolishing capital punishment. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 162, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 220}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The conclusion of the argument is that \"We shouldn't abolish capital punishment.\" This statement directly expresses the main point the argument is trying to make, which is supported by the premises regarding the consequences of abolishing capital punishment. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.91e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_98", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. The sense of a term is supposed to determine its reference. But reference can vary without any difference in thought. So, the senses of terms must be able to vary without variation in thought. So, our thoughts do not determine the meanings of our terms; meanings are not in the head. (Hilary Putnam)\n\nOptions: \nA. The sense of a term is supposed to determine its reference.\nB. But reference can vary without any difference in thought.\nC. Reference can vary without any difference in thought.\nD. Our thoughts do not determine the meanings of our terms; meanings are not in the head.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option summarizes the conclusion of the argument, stating that meanings are independent of our thoughts, as evidenced by the discussion about the relationship between sense and reference. The other options are premises that support the conclusion rather than being the conclusion itself.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 194, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 250}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option summarizes the conclusion of the argument, stating that meanings are independent of our thoughts, as evidenced by the discussion about the relationship between sense and reference. The other options are premises that support the conclusion rather than being the conclusion itself.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.269999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLU_formal_logic_40", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the conclusion of the following argument. That the world is my idea is a truth valid for every living creature, though only man can contemplate it. In doing so, he attains philosophical wisdom. No truth is more absolutely certain than that all that exists for knowledge and therefore this world is only object in relation to subject, perception of a perceiver. The world is an idea. (Arthur Schopenhauer, The World as Will and Idea)\n\nOptions: \nA. The world is an idea.\nB. That the world is my idea is a truth valid for every living creature, though only man can contemplate it.\nC. In doing so, he attains philosophical wisdom.\nD. No truth is more absolutely certain than that all that exists for knowledge and therefore this world is only object in relation to subject, perception of a perceiver.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The argument concludes with the assertion that \"the world is an idea,\" which encapsulates the main point Schopenhauer is making about the nature of reality as perceived by living creatures. This statement is the core conclusion drawn from the preceding premises regarding knowledge and perception.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 232, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 293}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The argument concludes with the assertion that \"the world is an idea,\" which encapsulates the main point Schopenhauer is making about the nature of reality as perceived by living creatures. This statement is the core conclusion drawn from the preceding premises regarding knowledge and perception.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.14e-05}}
